The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    protected function applyFix(\SplFileInfo $file, Tokens $tokens): void
    {
        foreach ($tokens as $index => $token) {
            if (!$token->isGivenKind(T_DOUBLE_ARROW)) {
                continue;
            }

            $this->fixWhitespace($tokens, $index - 1);
            // do not move anything about if there is a comment following the whitespace
            if (!$tokens[$index + 2]->isComment()) {
                $this->fixWhitespace($tokens, $index + 1);
            }
        }
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `PhpCsFixer\Tests\Fixer\ArrayNotation\NoMultilineWhitespaceAroundDoubleArrowFixerTest::testFix with data set #5`:
            
```php
    public function testFix(string $expected, ?string $input = null): void
    {
        $this->doTest($expected, $input);
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Code build on input code must match expected code.
Failed asserting that two strings are identical.
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
protected function applyFix(\SplFileInfo $file, Tokens $tokens): void
{
    foreach ($tokens as $index => $token) {
        if (!$token->isGivenKind(T_DOUBLE_ARROW)) {
            continue;
        }

        $this->fixWhitespace($tokens, $index - 1);
        // do not move anything about if there is a comment or whitespace following the double arrow
        if (!$tokens[$index + 1]->isComment() &&!$tokens[$index + 1]->isWhitespace()) {
            $this->fixWhitespace($tokens, $index + 1);
        }
    }
}
```
